Exercise 1 – Create a simple abstract class

Create an abstract class called Animal with:

one abstract method: makeSound()

one concrete method: sleep() that prints "Zzz..."

Then create two subclasses: Dog and Cat, each implementing makeSound().

Goal: understand basic abstract method implementation.

Exercise 2 – Constructors in abstract classes

Create an abstract class Vehicle with:

a field maxSpeed

a constructor that sets maxSpeed

an abstract method move()

Create a class Bicycle extending Vehicle.
Call the super() constructor and implement move().

Goal: understand how super() works with abstract classes.

✅ LEVEL 2 — Override rules & polymorphism
Exercise 3 – Covariant return types

Create an abstract class Document with an abstract method:

Document getCopy();


Create a subclass PDFDocument whose getCopy() returns PDFDocument instead of Document.

Goal: see covariant return types in action.

Exercise 4 – Polymorphic behavior

Create a Shape abstract class with:

abstract method double area()

concrete method double doubleArea() that returns area() * 2

Then create Circle and Rectangle subclasses.
In main(), create an array Shape[] with mixed shapes and print their doubled areas.

Goal: understand runtime method dispatch and leveraging concrete methods in abstract classes.

✅ LEVEL 3 — Multiple levels of inheritance
Exercise 5 – Abstract subclass chaining

Create:

Worker (abstract)

abstract method work()

Employee (abstract) extends Worker

implements work()

defines abstract method calculateSalary()

Programmer extends Employee

implements calculateSalary()

Goal: see that an abstract class can implement some methods but still remain abstract.

Exercise 6 – Template method pattern

Create abstract class Game:

final method play():

start();
playTurn();
end();


start() and end() are concrete

playTurn() is abstract

Create two games: ChessGame and CheckersGame.

Goal: learn template method pattern with abstract classes + final methods.

✅ LEVEL 4 — Realistic object modeling
Exercise 7 – Payment system

Create an abstract class Payment with:

field: amount

constructor

abstract method process()

concrete method validateAmount()

Create two subclasses:

CreditCardPayment

PayPalPayment

Each implements process() differently.

In main(), process multiple payments polymorphically.

Goal: abstract class for shared logic, different implementations for subclasses.

Exercise 8 – Device hierarchy with static behavior

Create abstract class Device:

static method powerInfo() returns "Devices use power"

abstract method turnOn()

Create Laptop and Smartphone classes.

In main(), call the static method from the abstract class and invoke turnOn() on objects.

Goal: understand that abstract classes may contain static methods.

✅ LEVEL 5 — Challenging
Exercise 9 – Abstract class + interface comparison

Create:

an abstract class Animal

an interface Pet

Animal has:

abstract method eat()

Pet has:

abstract method play()

Create Dog that:

extends Animal

implements Pet

Provide full behavior.

Goal: understand mixing inheritance + interfaces.

Exercise 10 – Framework-like architecture

Create an abstract class DataExporter with:

abstract methods: connect(), exportData(), disconnect()

final method runExport() calling the three steps in order

Create two exporters:

CSVExporter

JSONExporter

Simulate exporting data.

Goal: simulate the architecture used in real frameworks.